fungOS Mycelium-only qualification6 source bundle
================================================

This bundle is an aggregate. Each component retains its own license. fungOS
first-party code is MIT OR Apache-2.0; this is not a blanket license for Debian,
firmware, native libraries, compiler sources, or other dependencies.

Source directories:
  fungos              clean source 41ea743063f0bd9d7018f08227043bef47b03ba7
  mycelium            clean executable source 10a3c18ebea8b9f3f7be981657957ac10a5a2f16
  mycelium-packager    clean packager source f0980fba00412ed0772effc9a80d2d2446f3108b
  debian              587 exact source/version closures; DSCs and all SHA256 files
  debian-media-notices package-owned copyright/common-license texts from media
  debian-logo         original open-use SVG and separate upstream logo notices
  ubuntu-native       authenticated exact Zig and LLVM header source closures
  cargo-vendor        all 500 exact Cargo.lock registry source versions
  rust-library        actual Rust 1.98.1 library and compiler-builtins sources
  rust-notices        exact Rust library/toolchain attribution documents
  rust-llvm-libunwind  exact LLVM submodule 52ed14fcd56afc30f9cccd8ca8ce237c2eef7e04
  zig-runtime         materialized Zig 0.14.1 native runtime/include sources
  mycelium-notices    reviewed conservative notices, inventory and artifact binding

The vendor closure intentionally retains upstream tests and fixtures. Keys in
upstream cryptography tests are source fixtures, not fungOS fleet identities.
No enrolled guest disk, runtime claim, authority, private operator credentials or
fleet state is included. Source directories may contain extra target/build-only
code: availability is not evidence that such code is linked into the executable.

Manual build/runbook
--------------------
Use Linux with Rust 1.98.1, cargo-zigbuild 0.23.4 and Zig 0.14.1. Debian ISO
construction additionally needs xorriso and the tools listed in installer/README.md.
Build the executable from mycelium/ with its locked dependencies; to use the
included vendor source, pass Cargo configuration for source.crates-io.replace-with
and source.vendored-sources.directory pointing to the adjacent cargo-vendor/.

  cargo zigbuild --locked --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl \
    -p mycelium-cli --features iroh-sync

Read mycelium-packager/packaging/linux/README.md. Set
MYCELIUM_PACKAGER_SOURCE_COMMIT=f0980fba00412ed0772effc9a80d2d2446f3108b while
compiling that packager. Notice-only packaging of the retained qa5 executable
uses artifact version 0.1.0+qualification6 and executable source 10a3c18...,
with --third-party-notices pointing to mycelium-notices/. The executable's hash
is unchanged; the newer packager revision is recorded separately. If rebuilding
changes executable bytes, this notice binding must not be reused blindly.

Follow fungos/installer/build.sh and its component-bundle verifier using the
verified Debian 13.1.0 amd64 netinst input. Its required upstream SHA256 is
658b28e209b578fe788ec5867deebae57b6aac5fce3692bbb116bab9c65568b3.
The explicit mycelium-qualification mode is not a full Unibus/Canvas edge image.

SHA256SUMS binds every regular file in this bundle. Internal inventories bind
Debian/Ubuntu exact source versions and individual notices. This source bundle
does not contain release-signing keys and is not itself a signed release.
Publication still requires authenticated release metadata and publicly available
sources/notices. Engineering coverage is reviewed; legal clearance is not asserted.
